      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "There is no single consensus on this debate, as planners often balance the need for density to increase housing supply against the desire to preserve urban character and neighborhood cohesion. Advocates for density argue it is economically necessary to address affordability, while opponents emphasize that increasing housing costs dangerously can displace existing residents. Progress towards a compromise increasingly involves \"missing middle\" housing styles that add density without dominating entire neighborhoods, with local policy success highly dependent on community involvement.",
