      "content": "okay i get that there's a debate, but isn't the \"missing middle\" thing pretty much the clear winner here? like, if you look at the actual data on housing shortages and climate goals, adding density just seems like the objectively better path for a modern city compared to just keeping everything single-family. wouldn't you say density is the more logical solution for the future?",
